===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|eczemata|+}}

# {{lb|en|biology|medicine}} A [[non-contagious]] [[acute]] or [[chronic]] [[inflammation]] of the [[skin]], characterized by [[redness]], [[itching]], and the outbreak of [[ooze|oozing]] [[vesicular]] [[lesion]]s which become [[encrusted]] and [[scaly]].
## {{lb|en|usually}} {{synonym of|en|atopic dermatitis}} 
##: {{hyper|en|dermatitis}}
## {{lb|en|sometimes}} {{synonym of|en|dermatitis}} 
##: {{hyper|en|dermatosis}}

====Usage notes====
Usually, the word ''eczema'' refers to a specific kind of dermatitis, although the definitions of ''eczema'' and ''dermatitis'' are not universally standardized. For an explanation, see {{pedialite|Dermatitis#Terminology|Dermatitis § Terminology|nodot=1}}.

